Set `RULLST_PRIVACY_DATABASE` to the PostgreSQL connection URL of the
authoritative writable database (the generator selected the PostgreSQL store
because the project's primary database is PostgreSQL, or `--consent-store
postgres`). All application hosts must use that same database. Initialize it
once in a deployment step, with the variable exported into the process
environment:

```sh
cargo run --bin privacy-init
```

Initialization creates only an absent `rullst_consent` schema and validates an
existing one; it never resets or repairs state, and application startup only
connects. Ordinary `cargo run` still selects the main application binary. The
generated store has a 10,000 subject/tenant/purpose quota across the schema;
plan capacity explicitly before deployment. Expired choices and withdrawals are
not evicted automatically. Remote connections verify TLS; the runtime role
needs schema `USAGE`, `SELECT, UPDATE` on `metadata` and `SELECT, INSERT,
UPDATE` on `choices`. Replication, failover fencing and backup reconciliation
remain operator responsibilities.
